---
title: Baked Falafel
servings: 3
course: Main
source: https://www.bbc.co.uk/food/recipes/baked_falafel_with_09084
prep time: 30m
cook time: 1h
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Egyptian
---

Preheat the oven to 210°C and line a #baking tray{} with baking parchment.

Heat the @olive oil{1%tsp} in a #small frying pan{} over a medium heat. Add the @onions{2%small} and cook for about ~{10%minutes}, or until softened and starting to brown (add a splash of water if they start to stick). Remove from the heat and leave to cool.

Put the onions, @chickpeas{2%tins × 400 g}(rinsed and drained), @garlic{4%cloves}(grated), @cumin{3%tsp}(ground), @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @sea salt flakes{2%tsp}, @coriander leaves{30%g}(chopped), @flat leaf parsley leaves{30%g}(chopped), @plain flour{40%g}, and some @black pepper{}(freshly ground) in a #food processor{}. Pulse until the mixture is fairly smooth, stopping every so often to scrape down the sides with a spatula. Retain some texture but the paste should be able to hold together.

Divide the mixture into 18 equal pieces and shape into patties. Place on the prepared baking tray and spray or brush the patties with @olive oil{}. Cook on the top shelf of the oven for 20 to ~{25%minutes}, or until golden-brown.

Reduce the oven temperature to 180°C and move the tray of falafel to the bottom shelf. Bake for a further 20 to ~{25%minutes}, or until cooked through. Serve with @./Savoury/Tzatziki{}.